ΔH° = Σ ΔH°f(products) - Σ ΔH°f(reactants)

where ΔH°f is the standard enthalpy of formation.

For the given reaction:

CaO(s) + H2O(l) → Ca(OH)2(s)

ΔH° = [ΔH°f(Ca(OH)2(s))] - [ΔH°f(CaO(s)) + ΔH°f(H2O(l))]

Now, we can plug in the given standard enthalpies of formation:

ΔH° = [(-986.2 kJ/mol)] - [(-635.1 kJ/mol) + (-285.8 kJ/mol)]

ΔH° = -986.2 kJ/mol - (-635.1 kJ/mol - 285.8 kJ/mol)

ΔH° = -986.2 kJ/mol - (-920.9 kJ/mol)

ΔH° = -986.2 kJ/mol + 920.9 kJ/mol

