<USER_REQUEST>
Calculate the average radiation dose to the liver if 1.6 kg of liver tissue absorbs 0.12 J of energy from a radiopharmaceutical.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the average radiation dose to the living tissue, we need to convert the absorbed energy into a dose dose in Gray (Gy). The Gray is the unit of absorbed dose, defined as the energy absorbed per kilogram of material. The formula is:

\[
\text{Dose (Gy)} = \frac{\text{Absorbed Energy (J)}}{\text{Mass (kg)}}
\]

Given:
- Absorbed energy = 0.12 J
- Mass of liver tissue = 1.6 kg

Substituting the values into the formula:
\[
\text{Dose (Gy)} = \frac{0.12 \text{ J}}{1.6 \text{ kg}} = 0.075 \text{ Gy}
\]

The average radiation dose to the liver is 0.075 Gy.
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

