The index of refraction (\( n \)) is given by the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum (\( c \)) to the speed of light in the material (\( v \)):  
\[
n = \frac{c}{v}
\]  
Given that the speed of light in the plastic is 0.680 times the speed of light in a vacuum, \( v = 0.680c \). Substituting into the formula:  
\[
n = \frac{c}{0.680c} = \frac{1}{0.680} \approx 1.47
\]  
The index of refraction for yellow light in the plastic is \(\boxed{1.47}\).
