   - Molar mass of NO₂ = 14.01 (N) + 2 × 16.00 (O) = 14.01 + 32.00 = 46.01 g/mol  

2. **Use the vapour density formula**:  
   Vapour density (V_d) = (Molar mass of gas) / (Atomic mass of hydrogen)  
   Given V_d = 25.67, and  
   Molar mass of gas = V_d × Atomic mass of hydrogen = 25.67 × 1 = 25.67 g/mol  

