Using the two data points, we can set up two equations:

\[
\ln k_1 = \ln A - \frac{E_a}{RT_1} \quad \text{(1)}
\]
\[
\ln k_2 = \ln A - \frac{E_a}{RT_2} \quad \text{(2)}
\]

Solving for \( E_a \), we can solve the system of equations by solving (1) for \( \ln A \):

\[
\ln A = \ln k_1 + \frac{E_a}{RT_1}
\]

Substitute this into equation (2):

\[
\ln k_2 = \ln k_1 + \frac{E_a}{RT_1} - \frac{E_a}{RT_2}
\]

\[
\ln k_2 - \ln k_1 = \frac{E_a}{R} \left( \frac{1}{T_1} - \frac{1}{T_2} \right)
