where \(\mathbf{V} = V_x \mathbf{i} + V_y \mathbf{j} + V_z \mathbf{k}\).

For a 2D vector vector function \(\mathbf{V}(x, y) = P(x, y)\mathbf{i} + Q(x, y)\mathbf{J}\), the \(z\) component is \(\mathbf{V}_z = 0\). Thus, the curl is:
\[
\text{curl} \, \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial V_z}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial V_y}{\partial z} \mathbf{i} + \frac{\partial V_x}{\partial z} - \frac{\partial V_z}{\partial x} \mathbf{J} + \frac{\partial V_y}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial V_x}{\partial y} \mathbf{k}.
\]
Substituting \(V_z = 0\), we get:
\[
\text{curl} \, \mathbf{V} = 0 - \frac{\partial Q}{\partial x} \mathbf{i} + \frac{\partial P}{\partial x} - 0 \mathbf{J} + \frac{\partial Q}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial P}{\partial y} \mathbf{k}.
\]
Simplifying, we get:
\[
\text{curl} \, \mathbf{V} = \left( -\frac{\partial Q}{\partial x} \right) \mathbf{i} + \left( \frac{\partial P}{\partial x} \right) \mathbf{J} + \left( \frac{\partial Q}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial P}{\partial y} \right) \mathbf{k}.
\]
Thus, the coordinates of the curl are:
\[
\text{curl} \, \mathbf{V} = \left( -\frac{\partial Q}{\partial x}, \frac{\partial P}{\partial x}, \frac{\partial Q}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial P}{\partial y} \right).
